## Partials (`admin/partials/`)

Thin shells only — no business logic. Each page partial sets `data-launchdek-page` on `.launchdek-admin` root (including `settings`). Settings page uses Settings API form, not REST-driven CRUD.

Shared modal partials (require at end of page partial, do not duplicate markup):

| Partial | Included on |
|---------|-------------|
| `launchdek-onboarding-modal.php` | dashboard, settings |
| `launchdek-template-picker-modal.php` | dashboard, checklists, settings |
| `launchdek-confirm-modal.php` | sites |

Dashboard and settings include both onboarding + template picker modals (onboarding opens the picker from step 1). Checklists includes the template picker partial and inline auto-capture tab panel (no auto-capture modal). Sites page includes push checklist, connection tester, and confirm modals (confirm is shared partial; push/test modals inline).

## Client panel assets (`mu-plugin/launchdek-client/`)

Bundled mu-plugin admin UI — not loaded by hub `launchdek-admin` handle. Enqueued on remote wp-admin only when `LAUNCHDEK_Client_Run_Store::get()` returns an active snapshot.

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `css/launchdek-client-admin.css` | Panel styles — prefix `.launchdek-client-*` |
| `js/launchdek-client-admin.js` | Panel UI — IIFE, `launchdekClient` global (`restUrl`, `nonce`, `run`, `currentUser`, `strings`); uses `wp.media` for optional screenshot attachments; note collapse prefs in `localStorage` |

Key helpers: `buildClientApiUrl()` / `clientFetch()` — REST calls with plain-permalink `?rest_route=` fallback on `rest_no_route` (mirrors hub admin JS). `stepShowsNoteField()` / `stepShowsScreenshotField()` — gate note textarea and screenshot attach button from snapshot `show_note_field` / `show_screenshot_field`. `formatCompactProgress()` / `syncAdminBarProgress()` — keep collapsed layouts (sidebar tab, pill, toast, bars, fullscreen launcher, `admin_menu` trigger, `#wp-admin-bar-launchdek-client-checklist`) in sync on step toggles. `layoutKeepsPanelChromeOnCollapse()` — `inline_metabox` keeps panel chrome when collapsed (progress meta + **Expand** toggle). `applyOptimisticStepUpdate()` / `updateStepStatus()` — optimistic complete/uncomplete with rollback on error; hub callbacks return updated `run` (no redundant hub→client re-sync). Step complete/uncomplete posts `POST /client/run/steps/{step}/complete|uncomplete` → hub token route → applies returned snapshot via `save()` / `patch_from_hub_run()`. Per-step `.launchdek-client-step-notes-toggle` collapses individual note lists (prefs in `localStorage`).

Key panel classes: `.launchdek-client-panel-root`, `.launchdek-client-panel`, `.launchdek-client-panel-tab`, `.launchdek-client-panel-toggle`, `.launchdek-client-panel-collapsed-meta`, `.launchdek-client-admin-menu-trigger`, `.launchdek-client-step`, `.launchdek-client-step-settings-link` (compact deep-link icon beside step actions; URL from snapshot `deep_link` or rebuilt from `admin_path`), `.launchdek-client-step-notes`, `.launchdek-client-step-notes-toggle`, `.launchdek-client-double-tick-icons`, `.launchdek-client-icon-double-tick`, `.launchdek-client-note-attachment`, `.launchdek-client-run-complete-summary`, `.launchdek-client-dismiss-run`. Panel heading from snapshot `panel_title` (`LAUNCHDEK_Client_Run_Store::get_panel_title()`; hub setting `client_panel_title`). Layout modifiers on root/body: `.launchdek-client-layout-{sidebar|live_topbar|bottom_dock|floating_pill|toast|admin_menu|fullscreen|focus_mode|inline_metabox}` (legacy `left_sidebar` / `split_panel` fall back to `sidebar`); `body.launchdek-client-has-panel`. Modifiers: `.is-collapsed` on panel root/panel/step notes/metabox; `.is-completed` on steps. Completed runs show summary + **Dismiss** (`POST /client/run/dismiss`).

## Enqueuing

| Handle | File | When |
|--------|------|------|
| `launchdek-admin` (style) | `admin/css/launchdek-admin.css` | `is_plugin_screen()` |
| `launchdek-admin` (script) | `admin/js/launchdek-admin.js` | `is_plugin_screen()` + `wp_localize_script` |

Version: `filemtime()` when file exists, otherwise `LAUNCHDEK_VERSION`.
